G0907.def:
βαπτίζω 
(βάπτω), [in LXX: 4Ki.5:14 (טבל), Ésaïe 21:4, Jdth.12:7, Sir.31 (34)30 * ;] 
to dip, immerse, sink; 
__1. generally (in Polyb., iii, 72, of soldiers wading breast-deep; in i, 51, of the sinking of ships); metaphorically, to overwhelm (Is, l.with; cf. MM, Exp., x); with cogn. accusative, βάπτισμα β., Marc 10:38, 39 Luc 12:50. Mid., 
__2. to perform ablutions, wash oneself, bathe (Ki, Jth, Si, ll. with): Marc 7:4; aor. pass, in same sense, Luc 11:38. 
__3 Of ablution, immersion, as a religious rite, to baptize; 
__(a) (a) absol.; Marc 1:4, Jean 1:25, 26 28 3:22, 23, 26 4:2 10:40, 1 Corinthiens 1:17; ὁ βαπτίζων (= ὁ βαπτιστής, M, Pr., 127), Marc 6:14, 24; with accusative, Jean 4:1, Actes 8:38, I Co.1.14, 16; with cogn. accusative, τὸ βάπτισμα, Actes 19:4 (cf. Marc 10:38, supr.); pass., to be baptized, receive baptism: Matthieu 3:13, 14, 16, Marc 16:16, Luc 3:7, 12 21 7:29 (τ. βάπτισμα) ib. 30, Actes 2:41 8:12, 13 36 9:18 10:47 16:15, 33 18:8; mid., 22:16 (M, Pr., 163); 
__(b) with prepositions: ἐν, of the element, Matthieu 3:6, 11 Marc 1:4, 5 8, Luc 3:16, Jean 1:26, 31 33 3:23, Actes 1:5 2:38 10:48 11:16, 1 Corinthiens 10:2; εἰς, of the element, purpose or result (Lft., Notes, 155), Matthieu 3:1 28:19, Marc 1:9, Actes 8:16 19:3, 5 Romains 6:3, 1 Corinthiens 1:13, 15 10:2 12:13, Galates 3:27; with dative, ὕδατι, Luc 3:16, Actes 1:5 11:16; ὑπὲρ τῶν νεκρῶν, perh. to fulfil the wish of a dead friend, 1 Corinthiens 15:29 (see ICC, in l.; cf. DB, i, 238ff.; DCG, i, 169a; ii, 605b; Cremer, 126).
†

G0908.def:
βάπτισμα, -τος, τό (βαπτίζω), prop., the result of the act, τὸ βαπτίζειν, as distinct from βαπτισμός, the act itself, 
immersion, baptism; 
__1. metaphorically, of affliction: Marc 10:38, 39 Luc 12:50. 
__2. Of the religious rite of baptism; 
__(a) of John's baptism: Matthieu 3:7 21:25, Marc 11:30, Luc 7:29 20:4, Actes 1:22 10:37 18:25 19:3; β. μετανοίας, Marc 1:4, Luc 3:3, Actes 13:24 19:4; 
__(b) of Christian baptism; Romains 6:4, Éphésiens 4:5, Colossiens 2:12 (Tr., -μῷ, which see), 1 Pierre 3:21 (cf. Cremer, 130; Tr., Syn. §xcix).
†

G0922.def:
βάρος, -εος, τό, 
[in LXX: Juges 18:21 (כּבד), Jdth.7:4, Sir.13:2, 2Ma.9:10, 3Ma.5:47 * ;] 
weight; 
__(a) a weight, burden, lit. and metaphorically: Matthieu 20:12, Actes 15:28, 2 Corinthiens 4:17, Apocalypse 2:24; ἀλλήλων τὰ β., one another's faults, Galates 6:2; ἐν β., burdensome: 1 Thessaloniciens 2:6, R, txt., but see infr.; 
__(b) in late Gk. (Soph., Lex., see word), dignity, authority: ἐν βάρει, 1 Thessaloniciens 2:6 (R, mg.; see Milligan, ICG, in l.).† 
SYN.: ὄγκος, an encumbrance; φορτίον, a burden, that which is borne.

G0991.def:
βλέπω, 
[in LXX chiefly for ראה, also for פּנה, etc. ;] 
__1. of bodily sight; 
__(a) to see, have sight (opposite to τυφλὸς): Matthieu 12:22, Jean 9:7, Actes 9:9, Romains 11:8, Apocalypse 3:18, al.; 
__(b) to perceive, look (at), see: absol., Actes 1:9; with accusative, Matthieu 7:3, Marc 5:31, Luc 6:41, Jean 1:29, al.; ὅραμα, Actes 12:9; γυναῖκα, Matthieu 5:28; βιβλίον, Apocalypse 5:3, 4; τ. βλεπόμενα, 2 Corinthiens 4:18. 
__2. Metaphorical, of mental vision; 
__(a) to see, perceive, discern: absol., Matthieu 13:13, Luc 8:10; δι ̓ ἐσόπτρου, 1 Corinthiens 13:12; with accusative, Hébreux 2:9 10:25; before ὅτι, Hébreux 3:19, Jacques 2:22; 
__(b) to consider, look to, take heed: absol., Marc 13:23, 33; with accusative, 1 Corinthiens 1:26, al.; before πῶς, with indic., Luc 8:18, 1 Corinthiens 3:10, Éphésiens 5:15; before τί, with indic., Marc 4:24; before εἰς πρόσωπον, of partiality, Matthieu 22:16, Marc 12:14. Colloq. (for ex. from π., V. Deiss., LAE, 122; M, Pr., 107; MM, Exp., x; Milligan, NTD, 50), β. ἑαυτόν: Marc 13:9; before ἵνα μή, II Jo 8; β. ἀπό, Marc 8:15 12:38; before μή (cl. ὁρᾶν), with fut. indic., Colossiens 2:8, Hébreux 3:12; id. with aor. subj., Matthieu 24:4, Marc 13:5. 
__3. Of situation and direction (Lat. specto), to look, face (towards), places, etc. (before πρός, Xen, Hell., vii, 1, 17; Eze.40:23, 24): before κατά, with accusative, Actes 27:12 (cf. ἀνα-, ἀπο-, δια-, ἐμ-, ἐπι-, περ-, προ-βλέπω), see DCG, i, 446; ii, 596.
